<section class="card writer-tab-panel how-it-works"><h2>How It Works</h2><?=writer_subtabs($plotId,$tab,$subtab)?>
<?php if($subtab==='guide'):?><h3>How Story Writer Works</h3><p>Build a shared world in layers. Keep public facts separate from private knowledge, and make every important choice change what happens next.</p>
<div class="grid"><div><h3>Workspace tabs</h3><dl><dt>Story Framework</dt><dd>Define the premise, genre, locations, reusable story values, guided answers, cast size, and shared briefing without revealing private information.</dd><dt>Characters</dt><dd>Create each role’s public identity, private knowledge, goal, fear, starting location, and portrait.</dd><dt>Events</dt><dd>Place shared world events in chronological order. Events should advance the situation whether or not a player acts.</dd><dt>Decisions</dt><dd>Give a character a focused prompt, meaningful options, visible results, and mechanical effects. AI Rationale Guidance privately explains when an option fits the character.</dd><dt>Map, Dependencies, Opportunities</dt><dd>Use separate Map and Conditional Opportunities views to review dependencies and causal paths without a long scroll.</dd></dl></div><div><h3>Finishing the story</h3><dl><dt>Endings</dt><dd>Write condition-driven fragments covering the immediate result, character fate, wider aftermath, and a reason to replay.</dd><dt>Media → Artwork</dt><dd>Place story artwork beside a scrollable thumbnail library so images can be selected without leaving the workspace.</dd><dt>Media</dt><dd>Upload or reuse accessible images. Writers see only their own uploads; administrators see all active library media.</dd><dt>Submit for Review</dt><dd>Run validation and freeze the current story as a numbered revision for administrator and reviewer-assisted feedback.</dd></dl></div></div>
<h3>Make Decisions Interesting</h3><ul><li>Build dilemmas with real tradeoffs, not obvious good and bad answers.</li><li>Give each role only the information that character should know.</li><li>Let choices create visible narrative and mechanical consequences.</li><li>Use early details as later clues, leverage, risks, or reversals.</li><li>Allow branches to reconnect without erasing player agency.</li><li>Vary pacing between pressure, discovery, negotiation, and consequence.</li><li>Test every role, option, timeout, dependency, and ending condition.</li><li>Make the resolution reflect what players actually chose and protected.</li></ul>
<?php else:?><h3>Identifier Codes</h3><div class="identifier-guide-body">
<p class="help"><strong>A code is a permanent internal name.</strong> A label is the editable name a writer or player sees. A value is the current story state. Keep codes stable after another record begins using them.</p>
<div class="identifier-flow">Story → Event + Character → Decision → Option → Effect → Story Value → Condition or Ending</div>
<div class="identifier-grid">
<div class="identifier-item identifier-story"><h4>Story Code</h4><p>The parent namespace for the whole package. Example: <code>EMPTY_THRONE</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-location"><h4>Location Code</h4><p>Identifies a reusable place selected by characters and story logic. Example: <code>COUNCIL_CHAMBER</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-character"><h4>Character Code</h4><p>Identifies one role across decisions, opportunities, simulations, and revisions. Example: <code>ELIAN</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-event"><h4>Event Code</h4><p>Identifies a shared timeline event. Decisions attach to an event and a character. Example: <code>SEALED_ARCHIVE</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-decision"><h4>Decision Key</h4><p>Created by combining <code>EVENT_CODE|CHARACTER_CODE</code>. It means “this character's decision at this event.”</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-option"><h4>Option Code</h4><p>Identifies one response inside a decision. Its full key is <code>EVENT_CODE|CHARACTER_CODE|OPTION_CODE</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-opportunity"><h4>Opportunity Code</h4><p>Identifies a conditional decision that appears only when its conditions are met. Example: <code>ELIAN_SECOND_CHANCE</code>.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-choice"><h4>Dynamic Option Key</h4><p>Combines <code>OPPORTUNITY_CODE|OPTION_CODE</code> so an option remains unique within its opportunity.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-value"><h4>Target Code</h4><p>Identifies a managed Story Value changed by effects and checked by conditions. Its Effect Scope says where the value lives.</p></div>
<div class="identifier-item identifier-ending"><h4>Ending Section Code</h4><p>Groups alternate ending fragments by purpose. Reviewer keys combine <code>SECTION_CODE|PRIORITY</code>.</p></div>
</div>
<h4>Effect Scopes</h4><p class="help"><code>WORLD_STATE</code> shared facts · <code>FACTOR</code> story-wide measures · <code>STAT</code> character measures · <code>LOCATION</code> position · <code>KNOWLEDGE</code> learned facts · <code>RELATIONSHIP</code> connections · <code>GOAL</code> aims · <code>FEAR</code> risks.</p>
<h4>Value Types and Conditions</h4><p class="help"><strong>Numerical</strong> values show Default Numerical Value and use Change By. <strong>Preset Values</strong> show Allowed Preset Values and give effects and conditions controlled dropdowns. <strong>Free Text</strong> is for a short state that cannot be predicted as a fixed list—such as a discovered identity, named destination, or current objective—and effects show a Free Text Value field. A condition combines <code>SOURCE_TYPE + SOURCE_KEY + OPERATOR + VALUE</code> to decide whether an opportunity or ending is available. Changing a Story Value type or its allowed presets is blocked until every incompatible effect and condition named in the error is corrected.</p>
<h4>Code Locking</h4><p class="help">Gold fields are stable identifiers and appear first. A code stays editable until another record uses it. A locked field shows only compact dependency keywords such as <code>DECISIONS 2</code>, <code>EFFECTS 1</code>, or <code>ENDINGS 3</code>. Remove every listed dependency to unlock the code.</p>
<ul class="identifier-rules"><li>Use uppercase letters and underscores: <code>SEALED_ARCHIVE</code>.</li><li>Do not use spaces, punctuation, or a code already assigned to a different meaning.</li><li>Choose a short meaning that will still make sense when viewed outside this screen.</li><li>Once another record uses the code, edit the dependent record instead of renaming the identifier.</li></ul>
</div><?php endif;?></section>

